Got into Tekken back in Tekken 3 and been a fan since then.
Im not a hardcore player, so this is a list about what i've enjoyed from it so far :D
☑ Gameplay is fantastic, as you expect, but it feels they got it so much better this time;
☑ Storymode is awesome, prepare to git gud, even at medium final bosses are pretty tough;
☑ Gamemodes, both online and offline. You can have lots of fun gathering cosmetics;
☑ Online Matchmaking is functional and good;
☑ Superb graphics and sound;
☑ Combat is refined with new mechanics but still feels like good ol' Tekken;
☑ New Chararcters are fun and good to play with;
☑ Game has all the stuff you need to satisfy your nostalgia and more;
☑ IT'S TEKKEN ON PC.
It's a damn well made game, worth the price.

GREAT IF YOU LIKE: Interesting NPC dynamics; Satisfying gunplay; Open world faction warfare done right;
AVOID IF YOU DISLIKE: Crashing to desktop randomly; Grenade indicators;
This is the least good game in the incredible STALKER trilogy, and while it is a legitimate successor to the series' brilliance, I have to acknowledge that this is the weakest of the three games. What it does offer of the three is deepest and most developed faction warfare. As usual for STALKER games, NPCs are the crux of the games' brilliance: They are very intelligent, capable, and genuinely surprising in good ways. Here they are given more free roam of the map than in the other STALKER games, and some great stories can arise in unexpected interactions.
The game truly shines in its modding community, and I would recommend even brand new players seek bugfixes there before playing for the first time. Once modded, though, this is a truly fun open world RPG, even if overshadowed by the other two better games.

